  "summary": "RustyAttr is a macOS trojan, attributed to the Lazarus group, that uses the Tauri framework to build its application. The malware's primary TTP is to conceal a malicious shell script within a custom macOS extended attribute to evade detection. Upon execution, the script is read from the attribute and run to download a second-stage payload, while a decoy PDF or error dialog is shown to the user.",
